<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="sidebar_hud.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="sidebar_hud">
    <!-- Tier 7 sidebar HUD (game::draw_panels). A PERSISTENT, render-only,
         continuous every-turn document — NOT a modal open/loop/close screen. It is
         opened once during gameplay and synced each turn; modal screens stack above
         it by open order. The body is transparent so the cleared (black) sidebar
         region shows through; only migrated panels paint.

         Slice 2c owns Sound / Stats / Needs / Wgt-Vol / Mana. The owned panels are NOT
         contiguous in the layout (other panels can sit between them), so each fragment
         is its OWN absolutely-positioned element — game::draw_panels reports each
         panel's cell rect and sidebar_hud_position() places the matching element by id.
         Each fragment's text is built by its variant producer (g_hud_owned) +
         cata_text_to_rml() and bound to its model var. Further panels add their own
         element + var. -->
    <div id="hud-col" class="hud-col">
        <div id="hud-Sound" class="hud-panel" data-rml="sound_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Stats" class="hud-panel" data-rml="stats_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Needs" class="hud-panel" data-rml="needs_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-WgtVol" class="hud-panel" data-rml="wgtvol_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Mana" class="hud-panel" data-rml="mana_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Hint" class="hud-panel" data-rml="hint_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Movement" class="hud-panel" data-rml="movement_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Weapon" class="hud-panel" data-rml="weapon_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Armor" class="hud-panel" data-rml="armor_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
